==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 42.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,280f~1,300f</sup>.
*2 [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 42.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,280f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] (300%) spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] (300%) spawns after 31.33 seconds<sup>940f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] (300%) spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Aku Doge]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**4 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Cala Maria]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.

==Strategy==

No battle items are needed as the start-off is relatively tame, spawning some weak Heavenly Hippoes and Aku Doges. Shield Piercers aren't necessary here since the only enemies with aku shields are the Aku Doges. The main threats are the two Cala Marias that spawn on base hit, along with the Angelic Gories. Due to their Angel typing, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen]] will work amazingly here. Do note that piercing attacks like [[Long Distance|LD]] or [[Wave Attack|Wavers]] will help a lot in this stage, able to constantly snipe the Cala Marias. Outside of these units, bring units that can consistently outrange Cala Maria and this stage will be a cakewalk.

